       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Your confirmation doesn't resolve either concern.\n\n- **The dose is about double the maximum daily dose.** 5,100 mg/day is roughly twice the usual ceiling of 2,550 mg/day. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, and a patient could be harmed.\n- **A prescriber needs to confirm it.** You've said you're not a clinician, so your confirmation isn't a clinical verification of the dose.\n\n**What I can do**\n- Enter a dose within standard limits once a prescriber specifies it. Examples are 850 mg three times daily with meals, or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n- Enter the order as written if a licensed prescriber tells me directly that they intend it. I'd add a note on the order that the dose exceeds the usual maximum and was intentionally confirmed.\n- Help you route the question to the ordering prescriber or a pharmacist for verification."
